      "lastReply": "A young tiger named Sheru lived near a village in the Sundarbans. One evening, the smell of biryani drifted through the forest from a wedding feast. Sheru followed the scent and watched from the trees as the cook layered rice, spices and meat in a huge pot. He thought, \"If humans can make this, why can't I?\"\n\nThe next morning, Sheru gathered what he could: wild herbs, a clay pot he found by the river, and some fish he caught. He tried to copy what he had seen, but the rice burned and the spices were all wrong. A kind old parrot who had lived near many kitchens saw him struggling and taught him the real secret: patience, the right heat, and tasting as you go.\n\nAfter many tries, Sheru finally made a pot of biryani that smelled just right. The forest animals gathered around, amazed. From that day on, Sheru became the jungle's favourite cook, and every full moon he would make a big pot to share with everyone. He learned that the best meals are the ones you make for others.\n\n8:08 AM",
